From 24ac124a98f1e82babf6cce0a036d449f8f9b768 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:17:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] hub admission: drop no-op reservation filter, cover
 pickup() with a pool budget and legacy rows

The review reservation already falls back to ready rows in the same tick, so
filtering it by pool changed no outcome (no test could kill it): removed.
pickup() with a PoolBudget is now exercised end to end (a scalar <= check
raised TypeError), and a replica row without admission_class reads as normal.
Budget annotations widened to Any; design doc describes the per-pool budget.
---
 docs/kanban-hub-admission-v2.md                    |  8 +++++++-
 hermes_cli/kanban_db_dispatch.py                   |  2 +-
 hermes_cli/kanban_db_sync.py                       |  2 +-
 hermes_cli/kanban_worker_node.py                   |  4 ++--
 tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_hub_admission.py      | 10 ++++++++++
 tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_pickup_local_order.py |  3 +++
 6 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/kanban-hub-admission-v2.md b/docs/kanban-hub-admission-v2.md
index 203095bfd9..baee50bfb6 100644
--- a/docs/kanban-hub-admission-v2.md
+++ b/docs/kanban-hub-admission-v2.md
@@ -14,7 +14,13 @@ capacity-origin cap in final admission. Opt-in pre-lease/final CPU gates select
 separate priority pool. The dispatcher budget can reach the extra pool at regular
 saturation, preserving the shared critical/elevated memory guard. Opted-in hubs
 order marked candidates first within each lane, retaining effective priority
-within each group. Composed ready/review dispatcher tests now reach real final
+within each group. The dispatcher budget is per pool (`PoolBudget`): a normal
+row only fits a regular slot, so once this tick's regular slots are spent no
+normal row is attempted (no CPU advisory, Board claim gate or locked census),
+marked rows charge a priority slot first, and foreign pickup gets the same pool
+budget capped to the tick's total. At regular 7/7 the tick reports
+`at_capacity = "regular pool max_in_progress=7/7 (priority n/3 is marked-only)"`
+and a normal card's queue note says `regular pool full (7/7)`. Composed ready/review dispatcher tests now reach real final
 claims at 70% CPU with seven regular runs, including an opposite normal lane,
 critical/elevated memory and a hard per-board `max_spawn` ceiling. Workers retain
 plain priority. These isolated tests do not establish live acceptance.
diff --git a/hermes_cli/kanban_db_dispatch.py b/hermes_cli/kanban_db_dispatch.py
index e3030852a5..344da06540 100644
--- a/hermes_cli/kanban_db_dispatch.py
+++ b/hermes_cli/kanban_db_dispatch.py
@@ -2342,7 +2342,7 @@ def _dispatch_once_locked(
     # one slot back.
     ready_budget = spawn_budget
     if spawn_budget is not None and spawn_budget > 0 and _any_spawnable_review(
-        conn, [row for row in review_rows if pool_admits(result, row)],
+        conn, review_rows,
         per_profile_cap=per_profile_cap, per_profile_running=per_profile_running,
     ):
         ready_budget = max(spawn_budget - 1, 0)
